      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can solve this problem by analyzing and comparing the powers of $8$ that sum to $473$. The largest power of $8$ that is less than $473$ is $8^3 = 512$. Since $473 < 512$, it cannot be expressed as a single $3$-digit number in base $8$.\n\nTherefore, we need to express $473$ as a number of three-digit numbers. We can do this by dividing $473$ by $(8^3)$. However, since we only need the first digit of the base $8$ representation, we can halt the process as soon as we determine the first digit.\n\nWe can observe that $473/8^3 \\approx 0.00041625$, so we know that the first digit must be greater than $0$. It is also possible to verify this through a trial and error strategy, specifically through an equation: We can set this up as follows.\n\\begin{align*}\n473 - 0 \\times 8^3 & = 0 \\times 8^2 + n \\times 8^2, \\\\ 473 & = n \\times 8^2 + 0 \\times 8^1 + 0 \\times 8^0, \\\\ 473 & = 0 \\times 8^2 + n \\times 8^1, \\\\ 473 & = 0 \\times 8^1 + n \\times 8^0, \\\\ 473 & = n \\times 1, \\\\ n & = 473.\n\\end{align*}\nWe can conclude that the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473$ is $\\boxed{6}$.\nThe answer is: 6",
