      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we need to know whether it is positive or negative. Since $473_{10}$ is positive, we will convert it to base $8$. To convert a decimal number to base $8$, repeatedly divide the number by $8$ until the quotient becomes $0$. Keep track of the remainders at each step. These remainders, read in reverse order, become the base $8$ representation of the number. \n\n1. Divide $473$ by $8$ to get a quotient of $59$ and a remainder of $1$. \n2. Divide $59$ by $8$ to get a quotient of $7$ and a remainder of $3$. \n3. Divide $7$ by $8$ to get a quotient of $0$ and a remainder of $7$. \n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $731_{8}$. The first digit from left to right is $\\boxed{7}$.\nThe answer is: 7",
